Attribution, Reverse Engineering & Upstream Research Acknowledgments:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

OpenDSZ builds upon foundational protocol research and open engineering
contributions from the PlayStation reverse-engineering community:

1. Sony Interactive Entertainment Inc.
   - Linux kernel driver `hid-playstation` (drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c)
   - DualSense HID input and output report layout definitions.

2. daidr (daidr/dualsense-tester)
   - Research and documentation of Bluetooth Output Report 0x36,
     Opus audio encoding, and 3000Hz haptic PCM stream multiplexing.

3. nowrep (nowrep/dualsensectl)
   - Linux userspace DualSense HID communication architecture and
     IEEE 802.3 CRC-32 seed calculations for Bluetooth Report 0x31.

4. ligun0510 (ligun0510/PulseCore)
   - Concept inspiration for controller link diagnostics, 3.5mm jack
     headphone auto-switching heuristics, and master rumble attenuation.
